      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per discussion, can we only do this if the idletimer is enabled? It really doesn\u0027t make sense to tell BatteryStats about a network if it doesn\u0027t have an idletimer.\n\nI guess we can\u0027t change this without impacting T, but at least for U? We could do something like:\n\n    private IdletimerParams maybeCreateIdleTimer(int netId, int timeout, int type) {\n        if (timeout \u003c\u003d 0 || iface \u003d\u003d null) return null;\n        try {\n            final IdleTimerParams params \u003d new IdleTimerParams(timeout, type);\n            mActiveIdleTimers.put(netId, params);\n            mNetd.idletimerAddInterface(iface, timeout, getIdleTimerLabel(netId, type));\n            return params;\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n            loge(\"Exception in createIdleTimer \" + e);\n            return null;\n        }\n    }\n\nThen, in this code we can do:\n\n    final IdleTimerParams params \u003d maybeCreateIdleTimer(netId, timeout, type);\n    if (params !\u003d null || SdkLevel.isAtLeastT()) {\n        maybeUpdateBatteryStats();\n    }```suggestion\n            updateNetworkActivity(netId, type, true /* isActive */, NO_UID);\n```",
      "range": {
